ES is set up and `npx es run` passes (1 eval, 1 cell, 1 attempt).

### Layout

**`es.config.ts`** — fake harness, sandbox, and judge (no Docker or API keys):

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from '@invertase/foobar';
import { fakeHarness } from '@invertase/foobar/harness';
import { fakeJudge } from '@invertase/foobar/judge';
import { fakeSandbox } from '@invertase/foobar/sandbox';

export default defineConfig({
  harness: fakeHarness({
    files: { 'hello.txt': 'hello' },
  }),
  sandbox: fakeSandbox(),
  judge: { model: fakeJudge({ score: 1 }) },
});
```

**`evals/hello.es.ts`** — prompts the agent and checks the file deterministically:

```typescript
import { evaluate, expect } from '@invertase/foobar';

evaluate('hello', async (t) => {
  const turn = await t.send('Create hello.txt containing "hello".');
  await expect(turn).toHaveFile('hello.txt', 'hello');
});
```

**`package.json`** — installs `@invertase/foobar` from `/opt/es/invertase-foobar.tgz`.

The fake harness writes `hello.txt` on each turn; the eval asserts its contents with `toHaveFile`.
